The provided code is a C# class named `EncoderValidator` that is used to validate the version of FFmpeg installed on a system. The class has several methods, including `ValidateVersion`, `GetCodecs`, and `GetFFmpegFilters`, which are used to check the version of FFmpeg, get a list of available codecs, and get a list of available filters, respectively.

To write unit tests for this class, we can use the xUnit testing framework. We can create test classes that inherit from `EncoderValidator` and override the methods that we want to test.

Here is an example of how we can write unit tests for the `ValidateVersion` method:

```csharp
using Xunit;
using Moq;
using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;

namespace MediaBrowser.MediaEncoding.Encoder
{
    public class EncoderValidatorTests
    {
        [Fact]
        public void ValidateVersion_LogsError_WhenExceptionThrown()
        {
            // Arrange
            var loggerMock = new Mock<ILogger>();
            var encoderValidator = new EncoderValidator(loggerMock.Object, "ffmpeg");

            // Act
            var result = encoderValidator.ValidateVersion();

            // Assert
            loggerMock.Verify(l => l.LogError(It.IsAny<Exception>(), "Error validating encoder"), Times.Once);
        }

        [Fact]
        public void GetCodecs_LogsError_WhenExceptionThrown()
        {
            // Arrange
            var loggerMock = new Mock<ILogger>();
            var encoderValidator = new EncoderValidator(loggerMock.Object, "ffmpeg");

            // Act
            var result = ((dynamic)encoderValidator).GetCodecs(EncoderValidator.Codec.Encoder);

            // Assert
            loggerMock.Verify(l => l.LogError(It.IsAny<Exception>(), "Error detecting available {Codec}", "encoders"), Times.Once);
        }
    }
}
```

